From 2cdd5a6d9d2fa4129a8a28fa8ac62cb29e41c8da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frat <frat@pivotpoint.ai>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 10:38:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: responsive nav, active-page highlighting, hero overlap,
 mobile card overlap

- Navbar: add active-page underline/highlight driven by usePathname.
- Navbar: full desktop nav (links + search/lang icons) and hamburger toggle
  now switch at the same breakpoint (lg/1024px) instead of two different
  ones, fixing icon/link overlap and two-line wrap misalignment in the
  768-1024px gap (visible at 130% zoom, and on tablets). Real desktop
  widths unaffected.
- Navbar: nav labels are text-center so any wrapped label is centered.
- Hero: two-column split now kicks in at xl (1280px) instead of lg
  (1024px), giving the enlarged 69px 'REI AGINE' line enough room before
  the fixed 475px side column, fixing the overlap at 130% zoom / narrower
  laptop widths. Real desktop (>=1280px) unaffected.
- ServiceCard: title+description are now a single flex column instead of
  two independently absolutely-positioned elements, so a wrapped title on
  narrow mobile cards pushes the description down instead of overlapping
  it.
